WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.830
- So what were those first days like

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.077
'cause y'all were really young.

00:00:04.077 --> 00:00:04.910
- (Howie) Yeah.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.060
- Yeah I was 11 when I met these guys.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.020
- You were 11!

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.970
- I was 14.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.920
Yeah, I mean, back in the day,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.280
we used to ride on,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.990
basically like a Winnebago.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.690
We were doing what they
called this ESM tour.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.370
So we would go around to middle schools,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.990
high schools, gymnasiums.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:22.823
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:25.563
- Auditoriums, and perform music
that nobody had ever heard.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.960
We weren't signed yet.
- (Kevin) We did covers too.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.814
- Oh yeah, Of course

00:00:29.814 --> 00:00:30.647
- (A.J.) Covers and

00:00:30.647 --> 00:00:31.480
- Covers.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.550
- That's a hard play though to win over

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.140
like a high school crowd and like

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:34.973
- Totally.

00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:36.042
- We have some great stories.

00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:37.890
(all talking over one another)

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.030
Like even when you go to the school

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.170
and you're in something with the school

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.540
they're still mean like
it's like people are, yeah.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.720
- We were in I think it was
somewhere on the east coast

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.030
and we're in this auditorium,
we're doing our stuff

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.220
and the entire sound system went out.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.677
No mics, no nothing.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:53.623
- (Brian) They pulled the
plug like. (blowing raspberry)

00:00:53.623 --> 00:00:56.730
- So Brian is basically
trying to get everybody

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.340
to calm down and to stop
yelling and screaming.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.420
And they got really quiet

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.299
and we just sang straight
acapella and we won them over.

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:05.525
- (Kelly) Oh, I love that story.

00:01:05.525 --> 00:01:06.358
I was hoping it was going there.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.191
(crowd cheering)

00:01:07.191 --> 00:01:08.445
- (Nick) They were standing
up. They went crazy.

00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:09.278
- (A.J.) Yeah.

00:01:09.278 --> 00:01:10.254
- It was amazing.

00:01:10.254 --> 00:01:11.087
- (Kelly) You know what though?

00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:12.450
That's sometimes the better play.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.700
Like sometimes it's because
we always do like big things.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.470
I know people expect
like, big shows from you,

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.270
but it is those moments,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.440
and I don't know if Laurie agrees,

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.090
but it's those moments
when you do something

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.610
like really like, I don't
know, broken down like that

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.530
that really just
showcases the real talent.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.690
Like, you know, it's
kind of a cool moment.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:28.523
- Totally.

00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:30.390
- So that's probably why just
not everybody can do that.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.378
- Well, it shows that
you're real, you know?

00:01:32.378 --> 00:01:33.211
- (Kelly) Yeah, exactly.

00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:34.200
- What we do is, is real, you know

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.312
all five of us singing together.

00:01:35.312 --> 00:01:36.145
- (Kelly) Absolutely.

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:36.978
Just as you know, as a singer,

00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:38.781
I mean that's what we came to do.

00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:42.255
(all talking over each other)

00:01:42.255 --> 00:01:43.800
- (Howie) Harmonies. We've
always, since day one,

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.350
we've always picked up
songs, Boys II Men, Shy,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.970
Jodeci, Color Me Badd.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.400
We we loved the doo wop,
even, groups back in the days.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.317
We loved just picking
out all those harmonies.

00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.880
And that's what we got
our signature sound was,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.046
based around harmonies.

00:01:55.046 --> 00:01:55.879
- (Kelly ) That's so awesome.

00:01:55.879 --> 00:01:56.712
I'm glad you had that.

00:01:56.712 --> 00:01:57.780
Cause I'm sure we all
had those moments when

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.710
things went like that.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.450
And then we had moments
where they didn't go great.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.749
You're like, am I talented?

00:02:01.749 --> 00:02:03.146
And you have those moments.

00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:04.437
You're like, should I quit?

00:02:04.437 --> 00:02:05.970
And it's like, that was personally for me

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.920
when I saw U2 perform
Madison Square Garden.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.390
And I was like, what am I doing?

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.343
I was like, I should probably quit.

